   <text type="letter">
      <body>
         <div type="writingSession">
            <pb n="1"/>
            <opener><dateline><date when="1942-03-25">25 March 1942</date></dateline>
               <salute>Very dear <rs ref="#tillich_person_id__1928" type="person">Tillich</rs>:</salute>
            </opener>
            <p>I have yours of the 18th. It seems to me that <rs ref="#tillich_person_id__4304"
                  type="person">Mr. Manfred Saalheimer</rs> might find it of considerable interest
               to work out the religious biography of the members of his group and to study the
               changes of mind that result from their analysis and discussions. They might work out
               a questionnaire for private answers and they might keep a diary which at the end of a
               period they could analyze and interpret as a definition of the changing mind of the
               group.</p>
            <p>For a Jewish outsider&apos;s conception of anti-Semitism they might make use of essays in my book
            <q>Judaism at Bay</q> which I am sure the Canadian Jewish Congress would be glad to procure for them.</p>
            <p>I am returning herewith <rs ref="#tillich_person_id__4304" type="person">Dr. Saalheimer</rs>&apos;s
            letter<note type="ea">liegt nicht vor</note>.</p><closer>
               <salute>Yours</salute>
            </closer>
            <postscript><p><rs ref="#tillich_person_id__1928" type="person">Dr. Paul Tillich</rs><lb/>
            Union Theological Seminary<lb/>
            Broadway at 180th Street<lb/>
               <rs ref="#tillich_place_id__319" type="place">New York City</rs></p></postscript>
         </div>
      </body>
   </text>
